  "units": [
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "两人共话今昔种种事情，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "The two of them talked together about all sorts of things, past and present,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "源氏乘间说道：“内大臣想必天天都来探望，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and Genji, seizing a chance, said, \"The Minister of the Interior must surely come to visit every day,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "一天也不间断吧。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "without missing even a single day.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 4,
      "source_text": "倘得乘此机会和他见面，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "If I could take this opportunity to meet him,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 5,
      "source_text": "我真高兴呢。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "I would be truly glad.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 6,
      "source_text": "我有一事想告诉他，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "There is one matter I would like to tell him,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 7,
      "source_text": "然而没有适当机会，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "but there has been no suitable occasion,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 8,
      "source_text": "会面也不容易，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and meeting him is not easy either,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 9,
      "source_text": "叫我好心焦啊。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "which makes me terribly anxious.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 10,
      "source_text": "太君答道：“他么？",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "The elderly lady replied, \"Him?",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 11,
      "source_text": "大约是公事太忙，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Perhaps he is too busy with official business,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 12,
      "source_text": "或者是对我不甚关心之故吧，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "or perhaps he simply does not care very much about me,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 13,
      "source_text": "并不常常来访。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "for he does not visit often.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 14,
      "source_text": "你想告诉他的，是什么事情呢？",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "What is it that you wish to tell him?",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 15,
      "source_text": "夕雾对他确曾怀恨。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Yugiri certainly did bear resentment against him.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 16,
      "source_text": "我曾对他说：‘此事发生之初，情况虽然不明，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "I once told him, 'Although the circumstances were unclear when this matter first arose,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 17,
      "source_text": "但你现在厌恶他们，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "if you now despise them,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 18,
      "source_text": "硬把二人隔绝，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and forcibly keep the two apart,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 19,
      "source_text": "并不能挽回已经流传的声名，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "that cannot undo the reputation that has already spread,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 20,
      "source_text": "反教人纷纷议论，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "but will instead make people gossip all the more,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 21,
      "source_text": "当作笑柄。’",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and turn the matter into a laughingstock.'",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 22,
      "source_text": "但这个人从小有个脾气：",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "But this man has had one habit since childhood:",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 23,
      "source_text": "凡事一经想定，很不容易改变。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "once he has made up his mind about something, he does not easily change it.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 24,
      "source_text": "因此我也没有办法。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "So there is nothing I can do either.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 25,
      "source_text": "她以为源氏要告诉内大臣的是关于夕雾与云居雁之事，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "She thought that what Genji wished to tell the Minister of the Interior concerned Yugiri and Kumoi no Kari,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 26,
      "source_text": "所以如此说。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and so she spoke in this way.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 27,
      "source_text": "源氏笑道：“此事我也听到过，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Genji smiled and said, \"I have heard of that matter too,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 28,
      "source_text": "以为事已如此，内大臣或许不再干涉，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and thought that, since things had come this far, the Minister of the Interior might no longer interfere,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 29,
      "source_text": "慨然允许了。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "but would generously give his consent.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 30,
      "source_text": "因此我也曾经婉言劝请玉成其事。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "For that reason, I too once gently urged him to let the matter come to a happy conclusion.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 31,
      "source_text": "但我看见他异常严厉地申斥他们，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "But when I saw him rebuke them with extraordinary severity,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 32,
      "source_text": "便痛自后悔：我又何必插嘴呢！",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "I bitterly regretted it, thinking, why did I have to interfere?",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 33,
      "source_text": "我想：万事都可设法洗清，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "I thought: in all things, there may be some way to wash matters clean,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 34,
      "source_text": "此事难道不能洗刷，使它恢复原状么？",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "so could this matter not also be cleansed and restored to its former state?",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 35,
      "source_text": "不过在这恶浊可叹的末世，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Yet in this corrupt and lamentable latter age,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 36,
      "source_text": "要等待能够彻底洗清的水，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "to wait for water that can wash everything completely clean",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 37,
      "source_text": "也不是一件容易的事。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "is not an easy thing either.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 38,
      "source_text": "无论何事，在这末世总是越来越坏，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Whatever the matter may be, in this latter age it always grows worse and worse,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 39,
      "source_text": "越差越远。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and the gap grows ever wider.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 40,
      "source_text": "我听见内大臣为找不到好女婿而生气，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "When I heard that the Minister of the Interior was angry because he could not find a good son-in-law,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 41,
      "source_text": "对他很同情呢。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "I felt great sympathy for him.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 42,
      "source_text": "接着又说：“我要告诉内大臣的，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Then he continued, \"What I wish to tell the Minister of the Interior",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 43,
      "source_text": "却是另一件事：",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "is actually another matter:",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 44,
      "source_text": "有一个应该由他抚养的女儿，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "there is a daughter who ought to have been brought up by him,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 45,
      "source_text": "由于弄错情况，偶然被我找到了，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "but because of a misunderstanding, I happened to find her,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 46,
      "source_text": "抚养在我家里。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and have been raising her in my own household.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 47,
      "source_text": "当初并不知道弄错，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "At first I did not know there had been a mistake,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 48,
      "source_text": "所以我也不曾强要查明实际情况，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "so I did not insist on investigating the true circumstances,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 49,
      "source_text": "只因我家子女稀少，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and since children are few in my household,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 50,
      "source_text": "所以即使冒充，我也觉得有何不可，就容许了她。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "I thought that even if she were an impostor, there would be no harm in it, and I accepted her.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 51,
      "source_text": "我也没有好好抚养她，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "I have not raised her as carefully as I should have,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 52,
      "source_text": "一直过了许多年月。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and many years have passed in this way.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 53,
      "source_text": "但不知皇上何以闻知此事，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "But somehow the Emperor heard of this matter,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 54,
      "source_text": "曾经对我谈及。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and once spoke to me about it.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 55,
      "source_text": "他说：‘宫中没有尚侍，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "He said, 'There is no Naishi no Kami in the palace,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 56,
      "source_text": "内侍所的典礼常有怠慢。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and the ceremonies of the Naishi Office are often neglected.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 57,
      "source_text": "下级女官前来供职时，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "When lower-ranking court ladies come to serve,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 58,
      "source_text": "亦无人指导，以致秩序紊乱。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "there is also no one to guide them, so order has fallen into confusion.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 59,
      "source_text": "现有在宫中服务多年的典侍二人，以及其他相当人员，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "At present, two Naishi who have served in the palace for many years, along with other suitable people,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 60,
      "source_text": "频频前来请求，指望担任此职。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "come repeatedly to request the post, hoping to take up this office.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 61,
      "source_text": "但经严格考查，均非适任之才。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "But after strict examination, none of them proves fit for the role.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 62,
      "source_text": "故仍须依照古来惯例，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Therefore we must still follow the ancient precedent,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 63,
      "source_text": "选用门第高贵、人望隆重、而对私家之事不须兼顾之人。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and choose someone of noble lineage and high repute, who need not divide her attention with private household affairs.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 64,
      "source_text": "当然也可不拘门第，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Of course, one might also disregard lineage,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 65,
      "source_text": "专以贤能为标准而选择，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and choose solely by virtue and ability,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 66,
      "source_text": "使她因多年劳绩而升任为尚侍。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "promoting such a woman to Naishi no Kami because of many years of service.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 67,
      "source_text": "然而这类人现在也没有。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Yet there is no such person now either.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 68,
      "source_text": "因此还得从声望高贵的人家选出。’",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Thus we must still choose someone from a family of high standing and reputation.'",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 69,
      "source_text": "他暗中向我示意，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "He privately hinted to me",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 70,
      "source_text": "要选我所找到的女儿，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "that he wished to choose the daughter I had found,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 71,
      "source_text": "我又安可认为不当呢？",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and how could I regard that as improper?",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 72,
      "source_text": "凡女子入宫服务，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Whenever a woman enters the palace to serve,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 73,
      "source_text": "不论出身高下，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "no matter whether her birth is high or low,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02862",
      "unit_index": 74,
      "source_text": "总须按照自己身份而立志就职，",
